 "rationale": "The FBR failed due to diode drops (S2, S4) and lack of voltage regulation (S3). A Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) topology uses an inductor to flip the piezo voltage, significantly increasing the extracted energy and efficiency. I use a half-bridge SSHI with a rectifier to the output. A Zener diode is added to clamp the output voltage to 3.3V to satisfy the vmax <= 3.6V constraint for S3.",
